2. The number of benefits in force at time 0, which in turn is affected by:
i. the number of benefits in force during the year of the first layer,
i.e. the original model point
ii. the increase in number of benefits with each _year_ of new business
iii. the distribution of inception of benefits during the months of each year.
2 (ii) is determined by the entries in the array nb_policies_inc_mult, where
nb_policies_inc_mult[1]=1.0 and then nb_policies_inc_mult[i] is the factor by
which the total no. of benefits through the year increases from year (i-1) to (i)
2 (iii) is determined by the entries in the array nb_spread_multipli, where
nb_spread_multipli[i] is the percentage of benefits incepting in month
valn_month+(layer mod 12).
Note on layering: For each layer, MoSes starts the new business at time t=0.
It then displaces all the results for that layer by (layer) rows, sums these
"displaced" results for all the layers and shows this on the drill down.
Therefore formulae like proj_year need to be adjusted for each new business
layer to give the value at t=0 which will make sense when this has been
displaced by (layer) rows.
*/

